#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sqrt

#% text
# `sqrt(x)` gives the principal square root of `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `sqrt(x)` is the power `x^(1/2)`; there is no separate square-root head.

#% item
# Exact integers and fractions are simplified by taking out square factors: `sqrt(8)` is `2*2^(1/2)`.

#% item
# The square root of a negative number is imaginary: `sqrt(-4)` is `2im`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values; a negative machine real gives a complex number.

#% item
# `sqrt` is listable: it applies to each element of a list.

#% item
# `sqrt(x^2)` is not `x`, since that holds only for `x >= 0`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
sqrt(16)
#% output
#= 4

#% text
# Square factors are taken out:

#% cell
sqrt(8)
#% output
#= 2*2^(1/2)

#% text
# A negative argument:

#% cell
sqrt(-4)
#% output
#= 2im

#% text
# A machine number:

#% cell
sqrt(2.0)
#% output
#= 1.4142135623730951

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A fraction:

#% cell
sqrt(2/9)
#% output
#= (1/3)*2^(1/2)

#% text
# A ball, or 40 digits from the exact root:

#% cell
sqrt(2~40)
#% output
#= 1.414213562373095048801688724209698078570

#% cell
n(sqrt(2), 40)
#% output
#= 1.4142135623730950488016887242096980785696719

#% text
# Each element of a list:

#% cell
sqrt([1, 4, 9, 2])
#% output
#= [1, 2, 3, 2^(1/2)]

#% text
# A complex machine number:

#% cell
sqrt(4.0*im)
#% output
#= 1.4142135623730951 + 1.4142135623730951im

#% text
# Derivative and integral:

#% cell
d(sqrt(x), x)
#% output
#= 1/(2*x^(1/2))

#% cell
integrate(sqrt(x), x)
#% output
#= (2/3)*x^(3/2)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `sqrt(x)` is the same expression as `x^(1/2)`:

#% cell
sqrt(x) === x^(1/2)
#% output
#= true

#% text
# Squaring a square root gives the argument back:

#% cell
sqrt(x)^2
#% output
#= x

#% text
# Products of exact roots combine:

#% cell
sqrt(12)*sqrt(3)
#% output
#= 6

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# `sqrt(x^2)` stays as it is, because `x` might be negative or complex:

#% cell
sqrt(x^2)
#% output
#= (x^2)^(1/2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exp`, `log`, `abs`, `n`, `simplify`
